## Contributor License Agreement (CLA)

All contributions (agent uploads and model artifacts) to SN118 require a cryptographically signed Contributor License Agreement under the MIT License.

### 1. Check CLA Status
Check if your hotkey has signed the current CLA:
```bash
uv run ditto cla status
```

### 2. Sign the CLA
To sign the currently effective CLA using your registered hotkey:
```bash
uv run ditto cla sign --wallet default --wallet-hotkey default
```
The CLI displays the agreement, verifies the SHA-256 digest against Platform registry, and prompts for confirmation. The signature is verified and permanently stored.

### 3. Re-signing on New Versions
When a new CLA version is published, miners must re-sign using `uv run ditto cla sign` prior to their next submission.
